From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GE-Proton <git@localhost>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 22:15:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ds5: Publish simultaneous Sony controllers separately

The controller audio path historically assigned one canonical endpoint ID to
every controller of a given Sony model.  MMDevAPI then treated a second
physical controller as a duplicate and removed the first controller's PnP
AudioEndpoint registration.  Applications consequently saw multiple HID
controllers associated with one ambiguous audio endpoint.  Spider-Man lost
speaker effects and Assassin's Creed Shadows did not create haptic streams
until all controllers were removed and only one was connected again.

Retain the canonical endpoint ID for the first controller so the established
single-controller and hotplug behavior remains unchanged.  Give additional
same-model controllers a container-qualified endpoint ID, preserve that ID
across profile replacement, and keep it distinct in MMDevAPI's identity cache.
Also preserve every active Sony AudioEndpoint while registering another one,
and remove only the disconnected physical container during hot-unplug.

